dit's per-flow defect list\n51\t- Out of scope: screen-reader semantics beyond what the keyboard fixes\n52\t  require, and flows outside the four audited ones\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- Each of the four audited flows (project creation, workbench spawn, model\n57\t  deployment, pipeline run submission) can be completed end-to-end using\n58\t  keyboard only, and every defect enumerated in the audit report for that\n59\t  flow is verified fixed\n60\t- No focus traps remain: focus moves into modals when they open, returns to\n61\t  the invoking control when they close, and is never lost mid-flow\n62\t- Every interactive control in the audited flows is reachable and operable\n63\t  via keyboard\n64\t- Focus indicators are visibly consistent across all interactive controls in\n65\t  the audited flows\n66\t- A recorded keyboard-only walkthrough of each of the four flows documents\n67\t  the verification\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- **HLR-1 (P1)**: the four audited core flows fully operable by keyboard,\n72\t  with no focus traps or unreachable controls\n73\t- **HLR-2 (P1)**: visible focus indicators consistent across the audited\n74\t  flows — same remediation pass over the same flows and surfaces as HLR-1;\n75\t  bundled here because a split would re-audit the same controls twice\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a40f55888b7abdf6","agent_id":"a635cd8cfa9635a3b","session_id":"1febe4f8-5e51-4ce2-ab64-e380dbc0e05c","uuid":"78f0e3d2-1aa0-4a4c-9fe7-a719bb5917f4","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:06:12.704Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6c101f43e1f0b9c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9017 decomposition"}
